  "judgement": [
   "U vs R: the one-model reader names 5-7 known-kind letters on U upright, all 36 U pairs agree on 4-6, and the best-pair matches fall on one row (centre y std 0.12-0.14 mm, box height median 3.46 mm, x span ~15.7 mm) that recurs in all 3 triples (triple mean centres 0.04-0.09 mm apart); rotated 90 degrees the same pixels give 0-1 letters (R pair agreements 35 x 0, 1 x 1). This shows an orientation-specific, highly reproducible row-like feature that this reader names as letters.",
   "It does not show writing: a horizontal linear structure (fibre band or fold) is also orientation-specific, the reads come from one model, and matched namings coincide at a median 0.06-0.24 mm, so the 9 reads are strongly correlated and not 9 independent confirmations.",
   "Failing (i): the upright candidate agreement of 5 does not exceed what the same readers agree on in rotated census tiles. The null maximum 7 comes from two labelled-adjacent w010-027 tiles (census letters 10 and 8, rows Y, min distance to labelled segments 0 mm), one of them the candidate direct neighbour. They are very likely rotated real, training-adjacent text, and rotated text stays partly nameable.",
   "This makes (i) a strict, conservative comparator (stricter than a pure-chance null) but a correct one for the declared question. It was declared in advance with N0 drawn from all census tiles. The candidate sits beside that text region, and 5 agreed letters is inside the range this reader reaches on text-bearing material shown in the wrong orientation, so it is not diagnostic. Removing the neighbour tile leaves the null max at 7, and max U - P99 = -2 against a bar of 10.",
   "The subset maxima above are descriptive and post hoc; they do not bear on the outcome. The recorded outcome under DECL-P4-3 stands: not confirmed."
  ]
